About The Job
The CSIR has a vacancy for a Manager: Area Services in the Facilities Management and Security Services (FM&SS) department. The incumbents will lead and manage the provision of Facilities Management (FM) and Security Services (SS) to designated areas. This position is based in Pretoria.
Key Responsibilities
Leadership
Active member of the Facilities Services team with joint responsibility for developing and implementing the Facilities Services Strategic and Operational plans;
Develop, implement and drive the Facility Services plans for the CSIR;
Provide regular reporting to the Group Manager FM&SS;
Manage and develop staff to ensure high quality personnel who are able to achieve performance objectives in support of the CSIR mission and vision;
Conduct performance management contracting and reviews for all staff at the recommended periods, for the purpose of managing & improving both individual performance and service delivery.
Service Delivery
Responsible for planning, co-coordinating and managing all building infrastructure repairs and refurbishments for projects with up to a three-year period;
Manage and improve efficiency and effectiveness of FM&SS services delivery;
Optimise associated costs of service delivery;
Plan, coordinate and drive essential services such as accommodation/space requirements and relocation management; cleaning, hygiene and pest control services; boardroom and reception services; building inspections, maintenance and compliance; building safety, security and emergency systems and security services;
Develop, review and implement FM&SS specific procedures and processes;
Monitor and ensure the implementation and delivery of procedures and processes related to service portfolio responsibilities – responsible for delivering FM & SS KPIs;
Collect and analyse area calls logged for problems diagnosis to identify trends and implement corrective/appropriate action, including medium to long-term informed decision making on future strategy and plans;
Facilitate management and resolution of incidents, service complaints and other investigations related to FM&SS (facilities management, business support services, security, etc.);
Ensure the maintenance of building assets in accordance with the official investment strategy for each building asset;
Ensure the efficient and financially optimal maintenance of buildings;
Accountable for driving the Preventative Maintenance Program;
Ensure all buildings comply with all regulatory requirements.
Stakeholder Relationship Management
Actively engage in both internal and external stakeholder’s meetings related to FM&SS portfolio services e.g. Area management meetings, to influence and implement action plans, according to CSIR standards and policies;
Develop and implement business and operational plan for Facilities Services department in the designated area;
Facilitate and drive meetings with stakeholders for providing fit for purpose facilities, infrastructure and associated services;
Expert advice to stakeholders on best practice with respect to FM & SS practices and methodologies/ technologies, etc.
SHEQ Management
Ensure compliance with SHEQ regulatory requirements and standards in area of responsibility, including compliance by outsourced contractors/service providers;
Implement corrective action where deviations occur for the designated area;
Identify risks, implement, and drive mitigation plans for the designated area.
Management Responsibilities
Manage Area Services service delivery teams;
Manage, mentor, coach and play an advisory role for staff growth and development;
Conduct performance management contracting and reviews for all staff at the recommended periods;
Identify and implement training interventions;
Recommend and facilitate developmental plans;
Dispute resolution;
Ensure optimal resource deployment.
Financial management
Calculating and comparing costs for required goods and services to achieve maximum value for money and reduce wastage;
Managing and leading change to ensure minimum disruption to core activities.
Develop and manage budget for the designated area;
Planning and utilisation of space and resources for new buildings, or re-organising current premises for the purpose of optimisation.
Qualifications, Skills And Experience
A three year Bachelor’s degree, or equivalent, in facilities management or engineering, with at least five years’ management experience in facilities management and business support services, with a sound track record in:
Strategic and operational planning.
People management, including performance management. o Project management.
Financial management.
Resource planning and optimisation.
Understanding industry standards and regulations. o Customer service orientation.
