Background
The role sits within the Johannesburg Finance and Projects team. The Finance and Projects team carries out a wide range of work focused on the energy & infrastructure sectors, including project finance, internal investigations, front-end construction and sector-focused acquisitions and joint ventures in Africa. Our clients consist of a number of international banks, government entities, construction companies, infrastructure asset owners/sponsors and developers. This is a transactional and an investigative role which requires specialisation in the energy and infrastructure sectors, with a large amount of client contact. The role demands undertaking business development and marketing activities with enthusiasm.
The Candidate Required
This is a dynamic team where every team member can make his or her own mark. Associates are a key part of the team's development and are expected to take responsibility for leading on projects, energy and infrastructure focused investigation, developing and leading client relationships, contributing to the team's business development plans, focusing on sector activity and supporting the growth of more junior team members.
The role is wide-ranging, will focus on and include:
developing on-going relationships with an existing client base as well as pitching for new opportunities;
developing close working relationships as part of an international team;
the opportunity to be involved in internal investigation work within the energy and infrastructure sectors and on an international level;
taking an active role in our campaigns, the developments of our products and pitching for new work.
The successful candidates will:
have gained experience in a firm with an established energy and/or infrastructure practice;
have experience of project development transactions from a commercial and/or investigative perspective;
demonstrate experience of acting in a leading role in key transactions, being a self-starter and taking responsibility for client service;
be a team player, able to forge strong working relationships with colleagues;
be technically strong and exercise good commercial judgment;
be receptive to different ways of working including strong project management;
have interpersonal skills necessary for this client-facing role.
have experience in business development activities including presenting seminars or training sessions to external parties

Job Description
We are seeking an Administrator, reporting to an Assistant Manager within the Hedge Division of Sanne, to Conduct and maintain appropriate investor identification and verification, take ownership of and process investor transactions and deal with investor queries. This includes conducting and maintaining appropriate investor identification and verification screening mandated by the Sanne KYC Procedures prior to the opening of a new account relationship and ensuring this is consistent with the Sanne Fund Services SA AML Policy; and ensure all records are kept up to date. The incumbent will be allocated funds and will be responsible for ensuring all transactions are processed timeously and accurately while dealing with any Fund Manager or Client queries.
Key Responsibilities:
Perform KYC screening on new investors by collecting all required documentation on the investor as required by the KYC Procedures;
Establishing contact with the responsible external person and communicate Sanne requirements;
Assess documentation and information provided for completeness;
Follow up on outstanding requirements with Investors;
Confirm KYC sign off with internal Operational Teams;
Update and produce status reports as required;
Perform investor account refresh as required;
Ensure that the necessary documentation and information pertaining to the investors are captured and maintained in line with document retention policies
Administration of client matters;
Process subscription, redemption, switch and transfer instructions;
Maintenance of investor registers:
Process end of performance fee period transactions:
Create units for outstanding equalization credits;
Consolidate series funds;
Production and distribution of investor statements and investment certificates;
Servicing ad hoc requests for information; Provide creation/liquidation information monthly and distributing to fund managers;
Prepare and distribute income distribution statements;
Prepare and distribute provisional and year-end tax certificates – IT3B and IT3C;
Prepare and distribute ad-hoc reports including quarterly risk reports and audit certificates;
Record and monitor cessions applicable to investors
Establish excellent client relationships and provide high quality service and productivity;
Ensure that internal and external queries are dealt with timeously and professionally;
Liaise with internal departments for streamlined workflow;
Assist the external auditors to ensure the audit function is executed on a timely and efficient basis;
Requirements
Skills / Experience Required:
Grade 12 with Accounting or Mathematics (preferable);
1 – 2 years’ experience within the financial industry (preferable);
The ability to work in a fast-paced environment as well as multitask and re-prioritise on a regular basis;
Strong verbal and written communication skills;
Analytical and problem-solving skills with strong attention to detail;
Effective time-management skills to achieve deadlines;
Ability to work under pressure;
Excellent organisational skills;
Motivated and driven.

About The Job
The CSIR has a vacancy for a Research Group Leader in the Biomanufacturing Technologies (BT) impact area within Chemicals Cluster. The incumbent will be responsible for leading a team of scientists and engineers in developing and exploiting new knowledge, technologies and human capital to enable renewed development in the forest and waste biomass sectors. This position is based in Durban.
Key Responsibilities
Develop and implement a business plan for operation, sustainable growth, impact, and robustness of the biorefinery group including strategy, Research and Development (R&D) goals, HR, finances, technology transfer, IP and commercialization;
Lead a team of scientists, engineers, students, and interns to build and maintain a critical mass of skills in Biorefinery product and process development; ensure staff development and strategic Human Capital Development;
Promote a culture of science, engineering and technology (SET) excellence and provide multi-disciplinary RDI leadership;
Ensure that the Biorefinery team is dynamic, remains abreast of S&T and industry trends and remains innovative and internationally competitive in cutting edge R&D;
Build networks with peers in the fields of expertise within and outside the CSIR;
Deeply understand the needs of the industry by integrating sector knowledge in multi-dimensional research and development programs in order to deliver industry aligned RDI and assume leadership in the provision of technical solutions for these client programmes;
Engage with clients and industry partners to develop long term relationships;
Ensure that SET outputs are achieved; deliver on all KPIs of the area and ensure that all outputs are achieved, including transformation, financials, quality, health and safety as per agreed targets;
Implement and comply with appropriate financial and business systems requirements;
Provide technical support to business development activities and participate in client interactions, wwork closely with the Business Development and Commercialisation team to develop and package technologies for commercialisation;
Performance management of the staff members in collaboration with the Biomanufacturing Technologies impact area manager;
Be competent in and develop skills in process flow-sheeting, process integration, process optimisation, techno-economic assessment, process modelling and technology packages;
Manage infrastructure and equipment and the necessary set-up, implementation, commissioning, and safety of unit operations;
Ensure appropriate best practice and compliance with agreed quality and safety standards such as GLP, GMP, and execution of Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) to required performance requirements.
Qualifications, Skills And Experience
A Doctoral degree in chemical engineering or chemistry, with at least five years’ in a technology leadership role in product and product development, preferably in a Biorefinery environment or within industry in product and process development and commercialisation;
All international qualifications require an evaluation report / certificate issued by the South African Qualifications Authority (SAQA).
Professional registration will be advantageous;
A track record in successful technology development, transfer and implementation is essential;
Good people skills and experience in mentoring is essential;
Experience and a track record in securing funding for R&D projects in the public and private sector;
Sound experience in managing a team of multi-disciplinary professionals;
Proven track record in project management and research project leadership;
Business development and financial acumen;
Excellent communication, presentation skills, research and report writing skills;
Ability to provide thought leadership and high-level conceptualisation;
Ability to work independently as well as in teams;
Ability to convert industry/clients’ requirements to technical deliverables;
Ability to understand complete integration of technology to produce a functional product;
Problem solving, facilitation and interpersonal skills in a goal-oriented approach;
Conflict management skills, decisiveness, and action orientation;
Appropriate national and international RD&I networks;
An understanding of the research to market ‘innovation’ value chain.

